 2. What-is-it
 °°°°°°°°°°°°°
 SadoModem is an SMODEM implementation for CNet. SModem is a bidirectional
 transfer protocol with chat (YES, you can UPLOAD and DOWNLOAD and CHAT at
 the same time without any cps loss). Why not use Hydra? To put it simply,
 SModem is better than Hydra because with SModem you can add files to the
 batch during the actual transfer too. Another reason may be that most pc
 users won't bother to install Hydra if they already have SModem. 

 Q: But wasn't ZModem the top of the pops?
 A: Wake up, dammit! You're from texas or what? You'd make good
    pals with Metal$oft! I bet you think QWK is leading technology too?

 What does SadoModem do: 

    - Reads downloadlist from CNet's Selectlist
    - Modifies Ul/Dl credits according to ratios
    - Recognizes disabled ratios & freedl files
    - Recognizes subboards "New file validation" flag
    - Adds uploads to CNet's filelists internally
    - Gives upload time rewards
    - Skips the files user doesn't have enough credits to
    - Logging of transfers
    - Standard describing of files (can be disabled)
    - Should work on multinode systems (not tested)
    - Opens xfer screen on CNet screen if possible
    - Duplicate checking from multiple dirs
    - Supports CD-ROM temp dir
    - Uploads go to the subboards partition which has most free space

 And what not:    
    
    - Not nice. Adding files to filelists is a cruel hack.
    - No immediate upload testing or transformation
    - No upload resuming (currently aborted files are deleted)
    - Doesn't support CHARGES
    - Doesn't check if user is allowed to upload on this subdir
    - Doesn't increase download counters in filelists
    - Doesn't prevent downloading if not enough time left
    - Awholelot I don't know about


 3. Requirements
 °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°
 - SModem v1.0 (Amiga REV 4) or up (included) on path(!)
 - CNet 3.05c (Them hacks probably won't work with any other version)


 4. Installation
 °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°
 1) All SadoModem related files must be in Pfiles:SadoModem/ directory,
    except "SMODEM" which must be on command search path, eg. C:
 2) Create a subboard for SMODEM transfers ("Keep Buffers" must be NO and
    the subboard must not be located in a subdirectory!)
 3) Modify the SadoModem.cfg with a text editor to suit your needs.
 4) Modify dupecheck.lst to contain the full paths (one per line) you want
    to check (for preventing uploading of already existing files).
 5) Add this to BBSMENU ud/base section

    SModem      |#2pfiles:SadoModem/SadoModem}

 That's it.


 5. Usage
 °°°°°°°°
 Basically, SadoModem works in a similar fashion to the DS 
 (Download Selected) command.

 If SadoModem can't open or create the datafiles of its transfer
 subboard (_Items3, etc) when it wants to, shit will happen.


